      en: "Songnisan Mountain, meaning 'mountain of eternal sojourn', rises to 1,058 m in the Songnisan National Park, Chungcheongbuk-do. The park is home to Beopjusa Temple, founded in 553 CE, one of Korea's oldest Buddhist temples. The mountain features striking granite peaks and the 33-meter-tall Mireuk Buddha statue. The area hosts over 500 plant species, including rare orchids and endemic flora. The park was designated a UNESCO Biosphere Reserve in 1982.",
