      en: "Anmyeon Island is located off the west coast of South Korea in Chungcheongnam-do. As the sixth-largest island in the country, it spans 113.7 km² and is accessible via a bridge. The island is famous for its sandy beaches like Kkotji and the Anmyeon Pine Forest. The native Anmyeon pine is prized for making traditional Ssanghwa lacquerware. The island also features the Anmyeon-do Natural Recreation Forest, established in 1988. Fisheries, salt production, and tourism form the economic base of the island.",
